3655	/// truncated, only taking the first `n` bits:
3656	///
3657	/// > It will be silently truncated. In general, when storing value an integer
3658	/// > `I` into a segment of size `N`, the actual value stored will be
3659	/// > `I band ((1 bsl N) - 1)`.
3660	///
3661	/// <https://erlangforums.com/t/what-happens-when-a-bit-array-segment-size-is-smaller-than-its-value/4650/2?u=giacomocavalieri>
3662	///
3663	/// Thank you Björn!
3664	///
3665	fn truncate(literal_value: &BigInt, segment_bits: i64) -> BigInt {
3666	    literal_value & ((BigInt::one() << segment_bits) - BigInt::one())
